      "math_academy_id": "q-72305",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Given the hyperbolic paraboloid $(x+3)^{2}-2(y-3)^{2}=z-2$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $x$-intercepts of the paraboloid, we substitute $y=0$ and $z=0$ in the equation of the paraboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2}-2(0-3)^{2} & =0-2 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}-18 & =-2 \\\\ (x+3)^{2} & =16 \\\\ x+3 & =\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =-3\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solutions $x=-7$ and $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(-7,0,0)$ and $(1,0,0).$",
